     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><div>Hi all,<br><br>We&#39;ve just released the newest version (v2.9.0) of the <a href=\"https://github.com/stan-dev/stan/releases/tag/v2.9.0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/stan-dev/stan/releases/tag/v2.9.0&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793343066058000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3vwZwAw4sVsDBpZ6-iHaIx\">Stan</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/stan-dev/math/releases/tag/v2.9.0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/stan-dev/math/releases/tag/v2.9.0&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793343066059000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3ma9yQ5cZTNwoN18AfWTrM\">Stan Math</a> libraries (v2.9.0)!<br></div><br></div>Some of the new features in this release:<br>- General R-like indexing for arrays and vectors!<br>- Changed unit_vector transformation<br>- Better adaptation for ADVI<br></div><div>- New core developer member: Krzysztof Sakrejda. </div><div><br></div>For\r\n more details about this particular release, please see the full release\r\n notes: <a href=\"https://github.com/stan-dev/stan/releases/tag/v2.9.0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/stan-dev/stan/releases/tag/v2.9.0&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793343066059000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1_sum-Qaa-J57zVmvDm4uM\">https://github.com/stan-dev/stan/releases/tag/v2.9.0</a><br><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><div><br><br>The first interface to have the latest features is <a href=\"https://github.com/stan-dev/cmdstan/releases/tag/v2.9.0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/stan-dev/cmdstan/releases/tag/v2.9.0&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793343066059000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3dEJUz-Yddkxxh_BXWuicY\">CmdStan</a>. The release of CmdStan should be compatible with Stan.jl, MatlabStan, and StataStan.<br><br></div><div>RStan and PyStan will follow shortly.<br><br><br><br></div><div>-- Stan Development Team<br></div><div><br><br></div><div>P.S.\r\n The generalized indexing is really cool. Check out Chapter 5 in the \r\nv2.9.0 version of the manual: \r\n<a href=\"https://github.com/stan-dev/stan/releases/download/v2.9.0/stan-reference-2.9.0.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/stan-dev/stan/releases/download/v2.9.0/stan-reference-2.9.0.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793343066059000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1XNqd3NgK7WfOSDgnp3Q9D\">https://github.com/stan-dev/stan/releases/download/v2.9.0/stan-reference-2.9.0.pdf</a><br><br><br></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n"
